.TH CBMAP_CREATE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cbmap_create \- create a BST map with default settings
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cbstmap.h>

cbmap cbmap_create(ccol_data_type key_type, char **err);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Creates a self-balancing binary search tree map (AVL tree) that uses the
default memory management and the default comparison for the key type.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
key_type  Type of the keys that the map stores
err       Optional pointer that receives an error string on failure
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Returns a pointer to the new BST map on success
Returns NULL on failure
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Default comparison for char: the native char comparison of this
  platform, which is signed or unsigned to match the behavior of char on
  this platform
Default comparison for the other signed integer types: a signed
  integer comparison
Default comparison for the unsigned integer types: an unsigned integer
  comparison
Default comparison for float/double/long double: a numeric comparison,
  in which a NaN key sorts as greater than every non-NaN key and equal to
  every other NaN key
Default comparison for ccol_string: a strcmp-equivalent lexicographic
  order
The map keeps the AVL balance: |height(left) - height(right)| <= 1
All operations are O(log n) for a balanced tree
The caller must destroy the map with cbmap_destroy() after use
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cbmap_create_full (3),
.BR cbmap_create_mp (3),
.BR cbmap_create_ch (3),
.BR cbmap_destroy (3)
